<main id="main">
<section class="case-hero"><a class="back-link" href="/#work">← All work</a><p class="eyebrow">CASE 03 / PRODUCT STRATEGY · RESEARCH · UX</p><h1>Closing the loop between product evidence and better logistics workflows.</h1><p class="case-intro">A global logistics product supported vessel-related work across three regions. Performance monitoring and UX improvements were two connected fronts of the same project: understanding how the product was used, then using that evidence to shape its evolution.</p><div aria-label="Case at a glance" class="quick-read"><div><span class="quick-label">Challenge</span><p>Understand product use across regions and turn the evidence into priorities.</p></div><div><span class="quick-label">Contribution</span><p>Connect performance monitoring, user research and lead UX design.</p></div><div><span class="quick-label">Observed</span><p>NPS 40 → 78.2; 50 to 55% three-month retention, reported at programme level.</p></div></div><div class="case-metadata"><div><span>CONTEXT</span><p>Braskem · Global logistics</p></div><div><span>MY FOCUS</span><p>CX strategy &amp; analysis; Lead UX Designer</p></div><div><span>SCOPE</span><p>United States, South America &amp; Europe</p></div><div><span>TIMEFRAME</span><p>12-month monitoring · UX: Jan to Sep 2024</p></div></div></section>
<div class="case-cover source-cover"><button type="button" aria-label="Enlarge: KPI Monitoring" class="image-open laptop-frame" data-caption="KPI Monitoring"><img alt="KPI Monitoring" data-source-index="77" draggable="false" loading="eager" src="/assets/source-077.webp"/><span aria-hidden="true">Expand ↗</span></button></div>
<nav aria-label="Case sections" class="case-nav"><a href="#challenge">At a glance</a><a href="#decisions">Decisions &amp; project material</a><a href="#outcomes">Outputs &amp; outcomes</a></nav>
<div class="case-content">
<section class="challenge" id="challenge"><p class="eyebrow">THE BUSINESS QUESTION</p><h2>How do we turn product usage and user feedback into a roadmap that supports real logistics work?</h2><div class="contribution"><div><h3>My contribution</h3><p>Across the two workstreams, I worked on customer experience, data analysis and product strategy, and as Lead UX Designer for product improvements. I connected behavioural data and qualitative feedback to feature exploration, validation and design handoff.</p></div><div><h3>Collaboration</h3><p>Monitoring: Product Manager, CX Strategist, Change Manager and developers. UX: two UX designers, a Product Owner and the development team.</p></div></div><div class="facts"><div><strong>3</strong><span>regions using the product</span></div><div><strong>18</strong><span>survey responses</span></div><div><strong>5</strong><span>common pain points identified</span></div></div></section>
<div id="decisions">
<section class="chapter" id="decision-1"><p class="chapter-index">01 / DECISION</p><div><h2>Define what useful performance means</h2><p class="decision-summary">Connect business goals to HEART metrics and a monthly review rhythm.</p><details class="decision-context"><summary>Read the decision context <span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Stakeholder discussions connected product goals with the HEART framework: Happiness, Engagement, Adoption, Retention and Task Success. Monthly tracking combined behavioural analytics, satisfaction feedback and retention analysis. Frequency-based user groups helped the team explore different adoption and communication needs.</p></details><blockquote>Metrics needed context: who uses the product, for what work, and how often?</blockquote></div></section>
