<section class="chapter" id="decision-2"><p class="chapter-index">02 / DECISION</p><div><h2>Move from signals to design hypotheses</h2><p class="decision-summary">Investigate the signals with user feedback before committing to features.</p><details class="decision-context"><summary>Read the decision context <span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Microsoft Clarity data, interviews, surveys and benchmarking helped identify possible improvements. A survey gathered 18 responses and surfaced five common pain points. Information architecture and low-fidelity wireframes made ideas tangible before the team invested in detailed UI.</p></details><blockquote>A signal is a starting point for investigation, rather than a feature specification.</blockquote></div></section>

